BCE (bounds-check elimination)

Go emits `runtime.panicIndex` on `buf[i]` unless the compiler proves `i < len(buf)`.

Early abort + hint

```go
if len(data) == 0 {
    return errMalformedJSON
}
_ = data[len(data)-1] // BCE hint for data[i] in loop

n := len(data)
for i := 0; i < n; i++ {
    // ...
}
```

Window check before indexed loop

```go
if end > len(buf) {
    return ErrMalformed
}
for i := start; i < end; i++ {
    c := buf[i]
}
```

One early abort per buffer at loop entry is insufficient for nested indices; validate each sub-slice window.

Branch prediction

Prefer data-independent branches on hot path.

Presort + early break: RTB candidates sorted by score
Fast/slow path split: `if contentType == protobuf` before filter chain
Unlikely error last: Happy path first

Bitmask: `deviceMask & reqMask != 0`
Lookup table `[256]byte`: `jsonWhitespace[c]` in `requests_parse_opt.go`
`switch len(key)`: `matchTrackKey`
Packed compare: `loadU32(key) == u32Type`

Keep fail-open paths (geo, sampled metrics) off the critical branch chain.

Padding and false sharing

Cache line = 64 bytes on x86. Adjacent atomics without padding cause MESI invalidation.

```go
type IngressQuotaCell struct {
    maxAllowed uint64
    _          [ingressCacheLine - 8]byte
    currentOps atomic.Uint64
    _          [ingressCacheLine - 8]byte
}
```

Rules:

1. Pad hot globals with >= 2 contended atomics.
2. Use `cpu.CacheLinePad` or `64 - sizeof(field)` padding.
3. Do not pad read-mostly cold structs unnecessarily.
4. Prefer array of padded cells over `[]atomic.Uint64`.

Load atomics once per loop; prefer `atomic.Pointer` snapshot swap over per-field stores.

Escape analysis and inlining

- Struct layout: size-descending fields to reduce padding.
- No `[]interface{}` filter chains on `/track`; concrete `UnifiedFilter` short-circuit.
- Small hot loops: no `defer`; `//go:noinline` on cold error paths only.

unsafe.String lifetime

```go
func unsafeString(b []byte) string {
    if len(b) == 0 {
        return ""
    }
    return unsafe.String(&b[0], len(b))
}
```

View lifetime must not exceed gnet read frame. Values for async settlement require `copy()` into `evt.StringBuffer`.

Use `append(evt.StringBuffer[:0], b...)` instead of string `+`.

Pools and rings

vtproto `Event`: `sync.Pool` or package pools; reset on Get
MPSC rings: `FraudStreamWriter`, latency ring - fixed capacity, drop on overflow
gnet: `connContext` per connection; no global `sync.Pool` on request path

